exam: A farm accommodates chickens and rabbits, the aggregate number of heads being {h}. It is given that the rabbits possess, in total, {d4} legs more than the chickens. Determine the number of rabbits.
exam: Whereas a yard contains ducks and goats to the number of {h} animals in all, and the legs of the goats exceed in number those of the ducks by {d4}, ascertain the number of goats.
exam: State the number of tricycles in a yard containing solely tricycles and bicycles, given that there are {h} vehicles in total and that the wheels of the tricycles exceed in number the wheels of the bicycles by {d3}.
exam: It is given that a collection of spiders and beetles comprises {h} creatures, and that the spiders, each having eight legs, possess in aggregate {d8} legs more than the beetles, each having six legs. Determine the number of spiders.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left a farm of chickens and rabbits, {h} heads in all. The rabbits have {d4} more legs than the chickens. How many rabbits did he leave?
exercise: Last week the farmer culled some of the chickens. Now the farm has chickens and rabbits, {h} heads in all, and the rabbits have {d4} more legs than the chickens. How many rabbits are there?
